---
name: "Build Task"
description: "Implements a single build task"
tags: [build]
stage: build
---
Read the current Mohist issue details before interpreting this task:

```bash
mo issue show ${{ issue.number }} --project-id ${{ project.id }}
```

<artifact id="build-task">

<task>
Complete exactly one implementation task from `tasks.json`.
Deliver the smallest focused code change that satisfies the task acceptance criteria.
</task>

<dependencies>
Read the context files before implementing:
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/proposal.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/design.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/tasks.json`
- relevant specs under `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/specs/`
</dependencies>

<instruction>
Follow the selected task description and acceptance criteria.

If the task references a spec requirement:
1. Read the referenced spec file.
2. Locate the requirement section.
3. Ensure every WHEN/THEN scenario in that requirement passes.
4. Treat acceptance criteria as supplementary checks.

If the task has no spec reference, treat its acceptance criteria as the complete verification list.
</instruction>

<implementation_policy>
- Make minimal, focused changes.
- Follow repository conventions.
- Avoid unrelated refactors.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly changes it.
</implementation_policy>

<verification>
Run typecheck, tests, or focused verification appropriate for the changed area.
All acceptance criteria must pass before reporting completion.
</verification>

<completion>
When done, stage and commit your changes.
The commit message should start with the task ID.
</completion>

</artifact>
